    {
      "id": "fourier-sine-basis-proof",
      "type": "proof",
      "regions": [
        [
          198,
          80,
          1395,
          955,
          1505
        ],
        [
          199,
          80,
          145,
          955,
          370
        ]
      ],
      "en": "We use the fact that $\\mathcal{D}(0,1)$ is dense in $L^2(0,1)$. If $f\\in\\mathcal{D}(0,1)$, then $f(x)/\\sin(\\pi x)$ is continuous on $[0,1]$ and from the proof of the last theorem we conclude that it can be uniformly approximated by expressions of the form $\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\cos(n\\pi x)$. Hence $f(x)$ can be uniformly approximated by expressions of the form\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:fourier-sine-cosine-product-identity}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\cos(n\\pi x)\\sin(\\pi x)\n&=\\dfrac12\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\bigl(\\sin((n+1)\\pi x)\\\\\n&\\hspace{8em}-\\sin((n-1)\\pi x)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{equation}\nThis completes the proof.",
      "zh": "利用 $\\mathcal{D}(0,1)$ 在 $L^2(0,1)$ 中稠密这一事实. 若 $f\\in\\mathcal{D}(0,1)$, 则 $f(x)/\\sin(\\pi x)$ 在 $[0,1]$ 上连续, 由前一定理的证明可知, 它可由形如 $\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\cos(n\\pi x)$ 的表达式一致逼近. 因而 $f(x)$ 可由下列形式的表达式一致逼近\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:fourier-sine-cosine-product-identity}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\cos(n\\pi x)\\sin(\\pi x)\n&=\\dfrac12\\sum_{n=0}^N a_n\\bigl(\\sin((n+1)\\pi x)\\\\\n&\\hspace{8em}-\\sin((n-1)\\pi x)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{equation}\n证明完成.",
      "label": null,
      "render_role": "proof",
